const e={toc:[{id:"why-does-keratin-aftercare-matter",text:"Why Does Keratin Aftercare Matter?",level:2},{id:"the-first-few-days-what-to-do",text:"The First Few Days: What to Do",level:2},{id:"follow-your-stylists-washing-advice",text:"Follow your stylist's washing advice",level:3},{id:"avoid-tight-ponytails-clips-and-tucking",text:"Avoid tight ponytails, clips and tucking",level:3},{id:"keep-it-dry",text:"Keep it dry",level:3},{id:"sleep-gently",text:"Sleep gently",level:3},{id:"which-products-should-you-choose",text:"Which Products Should You Choose?",level:2},{id:"switch-to-sulphate-free-shampoo",text:"Switch to sulphate-free shampoo",level:3},{id:"use-a-matching-conditioner",text:"Use a matching conditioner",level:3},{id:"avoid-heavy-salt-and-clarifying-products",text:"Avoid heavy salt and clarifying products",level:3},{id:"add-a-light-leave-in-or-serum",text:"Add a light leave-in or serum",level:3},{id:"washing-habits-for-longer-lasting-results",text:"Washing Habits for Longer-Lasting Results",level:2},{id:"styling-after-keratin",text:"Styling After Keratin",level:2},{id:"swimming-sun-and-sweat",text:"Swimming, Sun and Sweat",level:2},{id:"chlorine-and-salt-water",text:"Chlorine and salt water",level:3},{id:"sun",text:"Sun",level:3},{id:"sweat-and-workouts",text:"Sweat and workouts",level:3},{id:"keep-hair-nourished-with-regular-hair-spas",text:"Keep Hair Nourished with Regular Hair Spas",level:2},{id:"when-should-you-book-your-next-treatment",text:"When Should You Book Your Next Treatment?",level:2},{id:"keratin-aftercare-mistakes-to-avoid",text:"Keratin Aftercare Mistakes to Avoid",level:2},{id:"keratin-aftercare-during-the-monsoon",text:"Keratin Aftercare During the Monsoon",level:2},{id:"a-quick-keratin-aftercare-checklist",text:"A Quick Keratin Aftercare Checklist",level:2},{id:"get-expert-keratin-care-in-bangalore",text:"Get Expert Keratin Care in Bangalore",level:2}],before:`<p>A keratin treatment can transform frizzy, hard-to-manage hair into smooth, glossy hair that styles in minutes. But how long that result lasts depends a lot on what you do afterwards. Good <strong>keratin aftercare</strong> is simple, and it makes a real difference to how smooth your hair stays over the following weeks.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>This guide covers what to do in the first few days, which products to use, how to style and swim, and how regular hair spas help. If you haven&#39;t had your treatment yet and are still deciding, start with our comparison of <a href="/blog/keratin-vs-smoothening-vs-straightening">keratin vs smoothening vs straightening</a>.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="why-does-keratin-aftercare-matter">Why Does Keratin Aftercare Matter?</h2>
<p>A keratin treatment smooths the surface of the hair to reduce frizz and add shine, while keeping your natural body and movement. Over time, the smoothing effect gradually softens as you wash and style your hair.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>Aftercare can&#39;t stop that completely, but it can slow it down. Harsh shampoos, hot water, chlorine and rough handling all wear the treatment away faster. Gentle habits help your results last longer.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="the-first-few-days-what-to-do">The First Few Days: What to Do</h2>
<p>The first days after your treatment are the most important. This is when your hair is settling into its new smooth finish.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<h3 id="follow-your-stylists-washing-advice">Follow your stylist&#39;s washing advice</h3>
<p>At the end of your appointment, your stylist will tell you when to wash your hair for the first time. Follow that advice, as the timing can depend on the treatment used. Washing too early can affect the result.</p>
<h3 id="avoid-tight-ponytails-clips-and-tucking">Avoid tight ponytails, clips and tucking</h3>
<p>Hair can take on a dent or kink easily while it settles. For the first few days:</p>
<ul>
<li>Avoid tight ponytails, buns and braids</li>
<li>Skip clips, bands and claw clips</li>
<li>Try not to tuck your hair behind your ears</li>
<li>Avoid sunglasses or headbands pushed into your hair</li>
</ul>
<p>Wear your hair loose and let it fall naturally.</p>
<h3 id="keep-it-dry">Keep it dry</h3>
<p>Try to avoid getting your hair wet in the rain, the gym or the shower before your first wash. Carry an umbrella, and use a shower cap. In the Bangalore monsoon, this is worth planning for.</p>
<h3 id="sleep-gently">Sleep gently</h3>
<p>Sleep with your hair loose and smooth. A silk or satin pillowcase reduces friction and helps prevent kinks overnight.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="which-products-should-you-choose">Which Products Should You Choose?</h2>
<p>Sulphates are strong cleansers. They&#39;re good at removing oil, but they also strip away the smoothing effect faster. A sulphate-free shampoo cleans more gently and is the single most important product change you can make after keratin.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<h3 id="switch-to-sulphate-free-shampoo">Switch to sulphate-free shampoo</h3>
<h3 id="use-a-matching-conditioner">Use a matching conditioner</h3>
<p>Pair your shampoo with a sulphate-free conditioner. Apply it to the lengths and ends rather than the scalp, and rinse well.</p>
<h3 id="avoid-heavy-salt-and-clarifying-products">Avoid heavy salt and clarifying products</h3>
<p>Clarifying shampoos and products with a lot of salt can be harsh on treated hair. Ask your stylist before using one.</p>
<h3 id="add-a-light-leave-in-or-serum">Add a light leave-in or serum</h3>
<p>A light leave-in conditioner or a few drops of serum on the ends help keep hair soft and add shine without weighing it down.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="washing-habits-for-longer-lasting-results">Washing Habits for Longer-Lasting Results</h2>
<p>How you wash matters as much as what you wash with:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use lukewarm water.</strong> Very hot water lifts the hair&#39;s surface and makes frizz return sooner.</li>
<li><strong>Wash a little less often.</strong> Many people find their hair stays cleaner for longer after keratin anyway.</li>
<li><strong>Be gentle.</strong> Massage shampoo into your scalp and let it run through the lengths, rather than scrubbing the lengths.</li>
<li><strong>Pat, don&#39;t rub.</strong> Squeeze water out with a soft towel instead of rubbing.</li>
</ul>
<p>If your water is hard, minerals can make treated hair feel rough sooner. Our guide to <a href="/blog/hard-water-hair-damage-bangalore">hard water hair damage</a> has tips that help.</p>
</details>
`,after:`<h2 id="styling-after-keratin">Styling After Keratin</h2>
<p>One of the best parts of keratin is how much easier styling becomes. A quick blow dry is often all you need. To protect your results:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>Always use a heat protectant</strong> before blow drying, ironing or curling.</li>
<li><strong>Lower the heat.</strong> Smooth hair needs less heat to style.</li>
<li><strong>Point the dryer downwards</strong> along the hair to keep the surface smooth.</li>
<li><strong>Use soft ties</strong> once the first few days have passed, and avoid tight elastic bands.</li>
</ul>
</details>
<h2 id="swimming-sun-and-sweat">Swimming, Sun and Sweat</h2>
<p>Chlorine and salt water can dry out treated hair and wear down the smoothing effect. If you swim:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<h3 id="chlorine-and-salt-water">Chlorine and salt water</h3>
<ul>
<li>Wet your hair with clean water before getting in the pool or sea</li>
<li>Wear a swim cap if possible</li>
<li>Rinse your hair with clean water straight afterwards</li>
<li>Follow with a sulphate-free shampoo and conditioner</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="sun">Sun</h3>
<p>Strong sun can dry out hair. Wear a hat or scarf on long days outdoors.</p>
<h3 id="sweat-and-workouts">Sweat and workouts</h3>
<p>Sweat is fine once the first days have passed. Tie your hair loosely with a soft band and rinse with lukewarm water afterwards.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="keep-hair-nourished-with-regular-hair-spas">Keep Hair Nourished with Regular Hair Spas</h2>
<p>Keratin smooths the hair, but your lengths still need moisture and care. A hair spa every few weeks keeps keratin-treated hair soft, nourished and shiny, and helps the treatment last longer.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>At Xing, every <a href="/services/hair-spa">hair spa</a> starts with a quick hair and scalp check, so your stylist can match the spa to your hair. A Nourishing or Moroccan spa often suits keratin-treated hair well.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="when-should-you-book-your-next-treatment">When Should You Book Your Next Treatment?</h2>
<p>Because keratin gradually softens over time, many people simply repeat the treatment as it wears off. Signs it&#39;s time:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li>Frizz is creeping back, especially in humid weather</li>
<li>Blow drying is taking longer again</li>
<li>Your hair has lost some of its shine and smoothness</li>
</ul>
<p>Your stylist can check your hair and advise whether to repeat keratin or try another option. If you want a different finish, our guide to <a href="/blog/what-is-nanoplastia">what nanoplastia is</a> explains another popular choice.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="keratin-aftercare-mistakes-to-avoid">Keratin Aftercare Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
<p>Most early fading comes down to a few common habits. Watch out for these:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>Going back to your old shampoo.</strong> If it isn&#39;t sulphate-free, it will wear the treatment down faster.</li>
<li><strong>Washing every day with hot water.</strong> Lukewarm water and a few less washes make a noticeable difference.</li>
<li><strong>Skipping heat protectant because styling is quicker.</strong> Smooth hair still needs protection from hot tools.</li>
<li><strong>Tying hair tightly in the first days.</strong> It&#39;s the most common cause of kinks and dents.</li>
<li><strong>Brushing roughly when wet.</strong> Use a wide-tooth comb and start from the ends.</li>
</ul>
</details>
<h2 id="keratin-aftercare-during-the-monsoon">Keratin Aftercare During the Monsoon</h2>
<p>Humidity is the main reason people book keratin in Bangalore, and the monsoon is when good aftercare matters most. Carry an umbrella, keep a small travel comb and a few drops of serum in your bag, and dry damp hair as soon as you can rather than leaving it wet for hours.</p>
<h2 id="a-quick-keratin-aftercare-checklist">A Quick Keratin Aftercare Checklist</h2>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ol>
<li>Follow your stylist&#39;s advice on your first wash.</li>
<li>Keep hair loose, dry and untied for the first few days.</li>
<li>Use sulphate-free shampoo and conditioner.</li>
<li>Wash with lukewarm water and handle hair gently.</li>
<li>Use a heat protectant every time you style.</li>
<li>Protect hair from chlorine, salt water and strong sun.</li>
<li>Book a hair spa every few weeks.</li>
</ol>
</details>
<h2 id="get-expert-keratin-care-in-bangalore">Get Expert Keratin Care in Bangalore</h2>
<p>Good keratin aftercare takes very little time, and it&#39;s the easiest way to keep your hair smooth, shiny and easy to manage for longer. Gentle washing, the right shampoo, heat protection and regular spas do most of the work.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>Book your <a href="/services/keratin-treatment">keratin treatment</a> at Xing Premium Unisex Salon in Sarjapur Road, HSR Layout or Brookfield, and every treatment comes with a complimentary Acai oil treatment and aftercare guidance from your stylist.</p>
</details>
`,takeaways:["Follow your stylist's advice on when to wash your hair for the first time.","Avoid tight ponytails, clips and tucking hair behind your ears for the first few days.","Switch to a sulphate-free shampoo and conditioner, and wash with lukewarm water.","Use a heat protectant every time you style, and be careful with chlorinated and salt water.","A hair spa every few weeks keeps keratin-treated hair nourished and helps results last longer."],faqs:[{q:"When can I wash my hair after a keratin treatment?",a:"Follow the advice your stylist gives you at the end of your appointment, as the timing can depend on the treatment used. When you do wash, use a sulphate-free shampoo and lukewarm water."},{q:"Why do I need a sulphate-free shampoo after keratin?",a:"Sulphates are strong cleansers that can strip the smoothing effect from your hair faster. A sulphate-free shampoo cleans more gently, which helps your keratin last longer."},{q:"Can I tie my hair after a keratin treatment?",a:"Avoid tight ponytails, clips and tucking hair behind your ears for the first few days, as they can leave dents and kinks. After that, use soft, loose ties."},{q:"Can I swim after a keratin treatment?",a:"Chlorine and salt water can dry out treated hair. If you swim, wet your hair with clean water first, wear a cap if possible, and rinse and condition straight afterwards."},{q:"Can I get a hair spa after keratin?",a:"Yes. A hair spa every few weeks keeps keratin-treated hair soft and nourished. Your stylist can recommend the right spa for your hair."}]};export{e as default};
